---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { ADS_ENABLED, ANALYTICS_CONFIGURED, withBase } from '../consts';
const updated = '8 November 2026';
// Every claim below is derived from the build flags rather than typed as
// prose. An earlier version of this page hard-coded "analytics is not
// configured yet" and became untrue the day GA4 went live, which is exactly
// the failure a policy page cannot afford.
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Cookies"
  description="Every piece of storage AI Audio Report uses, listed individually. By default that is one localStorage entry remembering whether you said yes to analytics."
>
  <h1 class="page-title">Cookies and local storage</h1>
  <p class="meta">Last updated {updated}</p>

  <p class="lede">
    Short enough to list in full, which is the point.
  </p>

  <h2>Set by default</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Lifetime</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>fr-consent-v1</code></td>
          <td>localStorage (not a cookie)</td>
          <td>Stores the single word “granted” or “denied” so the banner stops asking you. Never sent to any server.</td>
          <td>Until you clear your browser storage</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    That is the complete list. No cookies are set by this site unless you opt in.
  </p>

  <h2>Set only if you press Accept</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Name</th><th>Set by</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Lifetime</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_&lt;id&gt;</code></td>
          <td>Google Analytics 4</td>
          <td>Distinguishes visitors so we can count how many people read a page and which pages are worth expanding.</td>
          <td>Up to 2 years (Google's default)</td>
        </tr>
        {ADS_ENABLED && (
          <tr>
            <td><code>__gads</code>, <code>__gpi</code> and related</td>
            <td>Google AdSense</td>
            <td>Serves and measures advertising, and limits how often you see the same ad.</td>
            <td>Up to 13 months (Google's default)</td>
          </tr>
        )}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  {ANALYTICS_CONFIGURED ? (
    <p>
      Analytics is live. The script is fetched only after an explicit Accept, with IP
      anonymisation on and advertising storage, ad personalisation and ad user data all
      explicitly denied. Press Reject, or ignore the banner, and it is never requested.
    </p>
  ) : (
    <p>
      Analytics is not configured at the moment, so pressing Accept currently results in
      nothing being loaded.
    </p>
  )}

  <h2>Changing your mind</h2>
  <p>
    “Cookie settings” in the footer of every page brings the banner back. Choosing Reject
    stops the scripts from ever being requested; to remove cookies already set, clear site
    data in your browser.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  {ADS_ENABLED ? (
    <p>
      This site carries advertising supplied by Google AdSense. Ad units are labelled
      “Advertisement” so you can tell them from the writing. Nothing from Google's ad network
      is requested until you press Accept, and choosing Reject means no ad script is fetched
      and no advertising cookie is set.
    </p>
  ) : (
    <p>
      <strong>No advertising runs on this site today.</strong> No ad script is requested, no
      ad slot is rendered, and no advertising cookie can be set, whichever button you press.
    </p>
  )}
  <p>
    For transparency about what is coming: we have applied to Google AdSense and the
    application is under review. If it is approved, two labelled ad slots would appear on
    article pages, both below the article text rather than inside it.
  </p>
  <p>
    One thing worth stating plainly, because it constrains what we can do. Since 16 January
    2024 Google has required a certified consent platform integrated with the IAB
    Transparency and Consent Framework in order to serve <em>personalised</em> advertising to
    visitors in the EEA and the UK. The banner on this site is our own and is not certified,
    so until a certified platform is in place this site would be limited to non-personalised
    or limited ads. We would rather tell you that than imply a level of compliance we have
    not reached.
  </p>
  <p>
    Whatever happens, the rule does not change: nothing loads before you choose, and this
    page is updated before the behaviour changes rather than afterwards. The
    <a href={withBase('/privacy/')}>privacy policy</a> covers the rest.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
